# Root .env — deploy tooling only (scripts/deploy-web.mjs, ADR-0054). Gitignored; copy to .env.
# The reference server's environment is a DIFFERENT file: apps/server/.env.local (see apps/server).
# wrangler also reads a root .env / .env.local on its own, so this is the one place the id lives.
#
# The id of the Cloudflare account that holds the snugprotocol.org zone (`wrangler whoami` shows it).
# Auth itself is wrangler's OAuth session (`pnpm exec wrangler login`) — never put CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN here
# (wrangler would adopt it for every deploy).
CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=
#
# ONLY for `node scripts/deploy-relay.mjs ratelimit --apply` (the relay's WAF rate-limit rule, ADR-0064
# amendment 2026-09-04): an API token scoped to the snugprotocol.org zone with Zone.Zone:Read +
# Zone.Zone WAF:Edit. Wrangler ignores this name, so deploys keep using the OAuth session.
CLOUDFLARE_WAF_TOKEN=
